<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Amritsar (1846)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Amritsar of 1846 was an agreement by which the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> sold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh</a>, the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a>, for 7.5 million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupee">rupees</a>. It followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lahore">Treaty of Lahore</a>, which had stripped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> of Kashmir. Accounts of the Sikh Empire treat these settlements as stages in the empire's dismemberment.</p></div>
